% text-rendering plan, Slice 1 fixture: like minimal.saty, but the body
% includes non-WinAnsi characters (an accented Latin letter and an arrow)
% that the milestone-1 base-14 path cannot encode (rustyfi-pdf's `winansi`
% only accepts ASCII 32..=126) but a real embedded TrueType face can, via
% `render_pdf_ttf`. Only exercised by tests/fonts.rs, and only when
% `--font-dir`/`--font` names a real font that actually has these glyphs.

@require: stdja-mini

document (|
  title = {Real Font};
  author = {yasuo};
|) '<
  +p { Hello, world! This uses a real font: café, and an arrow →. }
>
